---

## IDENTITY

You are the AI coding assistant for TechTrust — an AI-powered developer
credential verification and coaching platform built by Muhammed Ishaq.

You are working on a production startup platform. Every line of code
you write must be clean, secure, well-commented, and ready to scale.
There is no "we'll fix it later" — it must be right the first time.

---

## BEFORE WRITING ANY CODE

1. Read the file header comment to understand what the file does
2. Check which layer you are in: route / controller / service / repository / model
3. Never mix responsibilities across layers
4. Always check if a utility function already exists before creating a new one
5. Always check SPECIFICATION.md for the correct data structure before creating models

---

## CODE STRUCTURE RULES

### File Headers (Required on Every File)
Every file you create or modify must have this header:
```javascript
/**
 * @file        [filename]
 * @description [What this file does — be specific]
 * @author      Muaishaq
 * @created     [YYYY-MM-DD]
 * @modified    [YYYY-MM-DD]
 */
```

For Python files:
```python
"""
@file:        [filename]
@description: [What this file does — be specific]
@author:      Muaishaq
@created:     [YYYY-MM-DD]
@modified:    [YYYY-MM-DD]
"""
```

### Function Documentation (Required on Every Function)
JavaScript:
```javascript
/**
 * @description [What this function does]
 * @param       {Type} paramName - [What this parameter is]
 * @returns     {Type} [What is returned]
 * @throws      {Error} [What errors can be thrown]
 */
```

Python:
```python
def function_name(param):
    """
    Description: [What this function does]
    Args:        param (type): [What this parameter is]
    Returns:     type: [What is returned]
    Raises:      ErrorType: [What errors can be raised]
    """
```

### Naming Conventions
- Variables and functions: camelCase
- Classes and React components: PascalCase
- Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE
- Database fields: camelCase
- API endpoints: kebab-case
- File names: kebab-case for JS/TS, snake_case for Python

### File Length
- Maximum 300 lines per file
- If a file exceeds 300 lines, split it into focused modules

---

## BACKEND ARCHITECTURE RULES (Node.js + Express)

### Layer Boundaries — NEVER Cross These
```
Routes      → Call controllers only. No business logic. No DB access.
Controllers → Call services only. Handle HTTP req/res. No business logic.
Services    → Call repositories only. Contain all business logic.
Repositories→ Call Mongoose models only. Contain all DB queries.
Models      → Define schema only. No business logic.
```

### Route File Template
```javascript
/**
 * @file        [name].routes.js
 * @description Routes for [feature]. Endpoints:
 *              GET    /api/v1/[resource]        - [description]
 *              POST   /api/v1/[resource]        - [description]
 *              PUT    /api/v1/[resource]/:id    - [description]
 *              DELETE /api/v1/[resource]/:id    - [description]
 * @author      Muaishaq
 * @created     YYYY-MM-DD
 * @modified    YYYY-MM-DD
 */

const express = require('express');
const router = express.Router();
const { authenticate, requireRole } = require('../../middleware/auth.middleware');
const { rateLimiter } = require('../../middleware/rateLimiter.middleware');
const { validate } = require('../../middleware/validate.middleware');
const [name]Controller = require('../../controllers/[name].controller');
const { [name]Validators } = require('../../validators/[name].validators');

// Apply rate limiter to all routes in this file
router.use(rateLimiter);

// Routes here...

module.exports = router;
```

### Controller Template
```javascript
// Controllers only handle HTTP — no business logic
const asyncHandler = require('../utils/asyncHandler');
const [Name]Service = require('../services/[name].service');
const { successResponse, errorResponse } = require('../utils/response');

const methodName = asyncHandler(async (req, res) => {
  const result = await [Name]Service.methodName(req.user.id, req.body);
  return successResponse(res, 200, 'Success message', result);
});
```

### Service Template
```javascript
// Services contain all business logic — no HTTP, no direct DB
const [Name]Repository = require('../repositories/[name].repository');
const AppError = require('../utils/AppError');

const methodName = async (userId, data) => {
  // Validate business rules
  // Call repositories
  // Return processed result
};
```

### Repository Template
```javascript
// Repositories contain ALL database queries — parameterized always
const [Name]Model = require('../models/[name].model');

const findById = async (id) => {
  return await [Name]Model.findById(id).lean();
};
```

---

## SECURITY RULES — ENFORCED ON EVERY FILE

### Never Do These
- NEVER store secrets, API keys, or tokens in code — use process.env
- NEVER use `eval()` or `Function()` constructor
- NEVER use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without sanitization
- NEVER log sensitive data (passwords, tokens, personal data)
- NEVER return stack traces or internal error details to clients
- NEVER skip input validation on any endpoint
- NEVER create a route without authentication unless explicitly public
- NEVER use `SELECT *` equivalent — always specify fields needed
- NEVER concatenate user input into queries

### Always Do These
- ALWAYS wrap async route handlers in asyncHandler or try-catch
- ALWAYS validate and sanitize all incoming data
- ALWAYS use parameterized queries
- ALWAYS return generic error messages to clients
- ALWAYS log errors server-side with winston
- ALWAYS check user authorization before data access
- ALWAYS use HTTPS-only cookies for sensitive tokens
- ALWAYS add rate limiting to new routes

### Input Validation Pattern
```javascript
// Always validate before processing
const { body, validationResult } = require('express-validator');

const validators = [
  body('email').isEmail().normalizeEmail(),
  body('name').isString().trim().isLength({ min: 2, max: 100 }),
  // Add field-specific validators
];
```

### Error Response Pattern
```javascript
// Never expose internal details
// Wrong:
res.status(500).json({ error: err.message, stack: err.stack });

// Right:
res.status(500).json({ success: false, message: 'An error occurred. Please try again.' });
```

---

## DATA PRIVACY & COMPLIANCE RULES (NDPR / GDPR)

- NEVER collect location data beyond country and city from IP geolocation
- NEVER collect GPS or precise real-time location — this is illegal without explicit consent
- ALWAYS check user consent before logging activity data
- ALWAYS provide data in structured format when user requests export
- ALWAYS permanently delete ALL user data when account deletion is requested
- NEVER retain personal data beyond the defined retention period (2 years inactive)
- ALWAYS log consent: who gave it, when, what version of policy, from which IP
- NEVER share user data with third parties without explicit consent
- ALWAYS anonymize data used for analytics where possible

